{
  "requirement": "The SDK formats node inputs using the domain's `format_node_content` method,\ndefined by {cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`:\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Method on Domain. Both arguments describe the already-read snapshot.\n/// Present these supplied contents as text for an agent.\nfn format_node_content(\n    &self,\n    node: &Self::NodeId,\n    contents: &Self::NodeContent,\n) -> Result<String, Self::Error>;\n```\n\nThe formatter uses the supplied contents; their fingerprint describes the same\nread. For inputs queued on an ask builder, formatting errors return\n`ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node` tool call, a formatting error is\nreturned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue and recover.\n`NodeContent` and `NodeId` retain their application-defined types without\nserialization or display bounds.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n**Formatting goes through `Domain::format_node_content`.**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` checks that the first chat message contains the formatted contents (\"source\").\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` checks that two nodes' formatted contents appear in the request in queue order.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` checks the order and repetition of rendered inputs.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` uses the `distinct_pages` formatter, which produces different text per node.\n\n**The formatter uses the supplied contents, and the fingerprint describes the same read.**\n- The `Memory` test domains in `agent.rs` and `validation.rs` can only format the `contents` argument. They cannot re-read.\n- The dependency assertions in the tests above (for example `Dependency::Node(.., fp)` with the matching value) tie the fingerprint to that same read.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` tests the real `HabeasDomain`. It supplies a snapshot for a file that does not exist on disk and asserts that the output contains the supplied text. A re-resolving formatter would fail on that missing file. The same test asserts that an unsupported node returns an error.\n\n**Formatting errors on queued ask-builder inputs return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` sets `fail_format` and asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`.\n- The same test asserts that no dependency was recorded and that the agent was never invoked.\n\n**A formatting error during a `read_node` tool call goes back to the agent as a tool error.**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[node_rendering_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` makes the formatter fail.\n- It asserts that the next request carries a `ToolResult` with `is_error`, the name `read_node`, and the error text.\n- It asserts that the agent continues and submits, so `ask` succeeds.\n- It asserts that the dependency list stays empty.\n\n**`NodeContent` and `NodeId` keep their application-defined types, with no serialization or display bounds.**\n- The `agent.rs` `Node` type is documented as having no Serde or Hash implementations.\n- `Contents` has no Serde or Display implementations.\n- These fixtures compile and run through the whole agent flow, which establishes the obligation at compile time.\n\nThe tests that cover this requirement all carry `{test}` references to `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`. The two other `Domain` implementations I found, in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]` and `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs`, panic if called. They show that edge-only and storage-only flows do not render contents. They are not needed for coverage. I found no gaps.",
  "references": "d3817100fa8b03f27dbb298688d80ca96a3f1c893a9c89d732f8d4c94879e24b",
